  "title": "The Month of Safar",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "al-Muhaddis al-Fayz and other scholars have mentioned that if you desire to be saved from the misfortunes and bad luck of the month of Safar, you may repeat the following supplicatory prayer ten times every day in this month:\nيَا شَدِيْدَ الْقُوٰى وَ يَا شَدِيْدَ الْمِحَالِ \nYAA SHADEEDAL QOWAA WA YAA SHADEEDAL MEHAALE \nO Lord of mighty prowess! O One of intense might! \nيَا عَزِيْزُ يَا عَزِيْزُ يَا عَزِيْزُ \nYAA A’ZEEZO YAA A’ZEEZO YAA A’ZEEZO\nO Almighty! O Almighty! O Almighty! \nذَلَّتْ بِعَظَمَتِكَ جَمِيْعُ خَلْقِكَ \nZALLAT BE-A’ZAMATEKA JAMEE-O’ KHALQEKA \nAll of Your creation is humbled before Your greatness, \nفَاكْفِنِيْ شَرَّ خَلْقِكَ \nFAKFENEE SHARRA KHALQEKA \nso suffice me against the evil of Your creation. \nيَا مُحْسِنُ يَا مُجْمِلُ يَا مُنْعِمُ يَا مُفْضِلُ \nYAA MOHSENO YAA MUJMELO YAA MUN-E’MO YAA MUFZELO\nO Beneficent! O Gracious! O Bestower of blessings! O Giver of bounty! \nيَا لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ سُبْحَانَكَ اِنِّيْۤ كُنْتُ مِنَ الظَّالِمِيْنَ \nYAA LAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA SUBHAANAKA INNEE KUNTO MENAZ ZAALEMEENA \nO One besides whom there is no god except You! Glory be to You, indeed I have been of the wrongdoers. \nفَاسْتَجَبْنَا لَهٗ وَ نَجَّيْنَاهُ مِنَ الْغَمِّ \nFASTAJABNAA LAHU WA NAJJAYNAAHO MENAL GHAMME \nSo We responded to him and delivered him from distress, \nوَ كَذٰلِكَ نُنْجِيْ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ \nWA KAZAALEKA NUNJIL MO-MENEENA \nand thus do We deliver the believers. \nوَ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِهِ الطَّيِّبِيْنَ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ.\nWA SALLAL LAAHO A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALEHIT TAYYEBEENAT TAAHEREENA.\nAnd may the blessings of Allah be upon Muhammad and his pure, immaculate family.\nAs for Sayyid Ibn Taaoos, he has mentioned a supplicatory prayer that is said at the sight the new moon of Safar.",
  "merits": "The Month of Safar is well-known for bringing bad luck; and nothing can remove bad luck except almsgiving, supplication to Almighty Allah, and traditional supplications of seeking His protection against Satan and bad things."
}
